{
 "_doc": "[PLAN 2a.5, 2026-09-11 — RUNNING_LOG §384] Every technique key the septet can write (the recipe keys of sandbox/instruments.js = the IR event `technique`), with its extraction FAMILY and its performer-facing NOTATION. classify.js reads `family`: oneshot -> class fixed-oneshot (the sample-true length from bank/sample_lengths.json where one is measured, else the drawn length with a warning — D9); sustained -> ord-sustained, or drawn-crescendo-curve when the note carries a multi-node envelope (morph notes classify as morph-note before either). A key NOT listed here still THROWS in classify (CL-5): a new recipe is added here, deliberately.",
 "_notate": "`notate` = the written instruction, where the composer has named one. null = NO MARK YET — stated, never a silent default; the notation of each technique is decided with him, note by note (the #4 method), and lands here. On 2026-09-11 exactly one is named: the flute `pizzicato` sample is written TONGUE RAM (composer 2026-09-04, RUNNING_LOG §44).",
 "_familyRule": "Generated once (2026-09-11) by ONE rule, then data: a key is `oneshot` when bank/sample_lengths.json measures it OR its name is a strike or a short note (pizz* · tongue_ram · stac* · spicc* · marcato_stac/spicc · slap · secco · key_click/noises · bartok · gettato · col_legno · finger · body · plucked · muted · harmonics (the piano's prepared harmonics) · fortepiano · sforzando); everything else — bowed, blown and held sounds, tremolos, trills, harmonic glisses, multiphonics — is `sustained`. Correct any entry by hand.",
 "_usedInPieceSeptet": "on 2026-09-11: senza_vel 235 · main 147 · gettato_vel 146 · bartok_vel 143 · slap 74 · pizzicato 72 · ord 50 · plucked 32",
